<!--
  Intraday Amplify sync, every 5 minutes, all day. Companion to
  com.grow.sr-sync — same cadence, same sleep behaviour (launchd coalesces
  missed interval firings into one catch-up run on wake).

  This is a headless Chrome run, not a bare HTTP pull like SalesRabbit, but a
  measured run is 11s wall / 2.6s CPU against Amplify's own portal, so 5 minutes
  is not a load anyone will notice. run-amplify-sync.sh holds a pid lock and
  kills a run at 4 minutes, under the interval, so a hung Chrome costs one
  skipped tick rather than wedging the schedule.

  If you change this, change `every:` and `sched:` on the 'tds' row in
  index.html (_growSyncStatus) too — the health board measures "runs missed"
  against that number.

  Kept as a SEPARATE agent rather than folded into the SalesRabbit runner so the
  two fail independently: an expired SalesRabbit token must not stop Amplify
  from syncing, and vice versa.

  Install:
    cp scripts/launchd/com.grow.amplify-sync.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.grow.amplify-sync.plist
  Check:   launchctl list | grep amplify-sync
  Remove:  launchctl unload ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.grow.amplify-sync.plist
-->
